# rule.always.converge-with-reviewers.via-a-taken-per-point

for EVERY `.given.by_peer` point you MUST author the paired `.taken.by_self` before you re-arrive. no exceptions, every round.

the reviewer drops a point that carries a response and **re-raises one that does not** — so a code fix with no `.taken` reads to it as no fix at all.

| shape | the claim | must carry |
|---|---|---|
| `[REPAIR]` | *"i fixed it"* | a quote of the **current** file |
| `[REFUTE]` | *"it does not hold"* | cited evidence — out of scope, a false positive, a deliberate tradeoff |

then, per point: `rhx route.stone.set --stone <stone> --as absorbed --that <slug>` — and only then re-arrive.

a blocker that returns after you fixed it is a driver error, never a reviewer defect. check
whether you ever told the reviewer, before you diagnose one.

## the gate counts REVIEWERS. this rule counts POINTS

the entrance gate refuses a round while a reviewer owes a `.taken`. it cannot check that the one
file you wrote answered all six points behind that slug — one `.taken` discharges the slug
regardless. the gate enforces the parent rule, never this one. a round that passes the door can
still violate every line above, and the reviewer — which does count points — re-raises each one
you skipped. the door is a floor; this rule is the work.

## on an APPROVED lane the floor is ZERO — the gate holds naught, and the tool says so

the gate keys on a rejected lane's debt, so a lane that returned `0 blockers` with nitpicks has
no gate at all. the reviewer still weighs points, and re-raises every nitpick that carries no
response. `approved` grades the lane, never the points.

`--as absorbed --that <slug>` there, with no `.taken`, absorbs and warns *"its nitpicks carry no
.taken"*, with the path the answer belongs at. it warns; it does not refuse.

only a `.taken` discharges a point. on an approved lane you are the sole enforcement, so the
rule binds hardest exactly where the engine binds least.

measured 2026-09-21 (`rhachet-roles-bhrain` @ `beav/feat-review-cost-meter`, stone `1.vision`):
approved at i001 and i002, five re-raises, zero takens — every report read "no repair present."
one round with takens: 0 blockers, 0 nitpicks, both lanes.

blocker: an open point with no `.taken` · a `[REPAIR]` with no current-file quote · a `[REFUTE]`
with no evidence · a malfunction graded for a re-raise you never answered · a re-arrival with an
open point from an approved lane that has no `.taken`.

the forbid twin is `rule.forbid.unanswered-exits-from-a-blocker`: this rule says every point
owes a `.taken`; that one shuts the other doors out of a blocker.
